    },
    {
      "id": "3iec-standard-indices-q09",
      "section": "Indices — Foundation",
      "title": "9",
      "prompt": "Simplify \\(a^4\\times a^5\\).",
      "options": [
        "\\(a^{20}\\)",
        "\\(a^9\\)",
        "\\(2a^9\\)",
        "\\(a\\)"
      ],
      "answer": 1,
      "solution": "\\(a^9\\)",
      "working": "<p>When multiplying powers with the same base, add the indices.</p>\\[a^4\\times a^5=a^{4+5}=a^9.\\]",
      "source_ref": "Original"
    },
    {
      "id": "3iec-standard-indices-q10",
      "section": "Indices — Foundation",
      "title": "10",
      "prompt": "For \\(x\\ne0\\), simplify \\(\\frac{x^3}{x^8}\\) using a positive index.",
      "options": [
        "\\(x^5\\)",
        "\\(\\frac{1}{x^{11}}\\)",
        "\\(\\frac{1}{x^5}\\)",
        "\\(\\frac{1}{5x}\\)"
      ],
      "answer": 2,
      "solution": "\\(\\frac{1}{x^5}\\)",
      "working": "<p>Subtract the indices, then use the reciprocal for a negative index.</p>\\[\\frac{x^3}{x^8}=x^{3-8}=x^{-5}=\\frac{1}{x^5}.\\]",
      "source_ref": "Original"
    },
    {
