      ],
      "answer": 2,
      "solution": "\\(\\frac32\\)",
      "working": "<p>Write both sides as powers of 2.</p>\\[(2^2)^{x+1}=2^5\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad2(x+1)=5.\\]<p>Thus \\(2x=3\\), giving \\(x=\\frac{3}{2}\\).</p>",
      "source_ref": "Original"
